  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Construction of a two storey side extension, a single storey rear extension and a front porch",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;The proposed two-storey side extension, by reason of its bulk, mass, scale, siting and design, would present an significant and undesirable addition to the host dwelling, which would result in the dwelling being disproportionately large in comparison to the other dwellings along the host terrace row and surrounding dwellings, unbalance the symmetry and uniformity across the host terrace row, diminish the open corner plot at the entrance to the banjo cul-de-sac. For these reasons, the proposal is would be at odds with the character and appearance of the area, notably given the location of the application site within the Becontree Estate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;As such, the proposed development is contrary to: - National Planning Policy Framework &amp;nbsp;(NPPF) (December 2024) - Polies D1, D4, D5, D6 and HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) -&amp;nbsp; Policies&amp;nbsp; DMD1, DMD4, DMD5,&amp;nbsp; SP2 and SPP6 of&amp;nbsp; the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024) - The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
